{
  "id": "ui-sticky-nav",
  "title": "Sticky nav: a header band that stays put while the page scrolls, on a canvas with no position offsets",
  "description": "Position and stacking without top/left/right/bottom ports — and it IS authorable. Every visual node carries a `position` port; set the header band to \"sticky\" and it holds the top edge while the page scrolls under it (measured: the band's viewport top stays 0 at scrollTop 305 of 1205 at 1280px, and 811 of 1655 at 390px). Four things decide whether it works. (1) THE INSET COMES FROM `alignY`, because no `top` port exists: for any non-relative position `alignY` already defaults to \"top\" and that is what writes `top: 0` — declare it so the intent is visible, and never set it to \"center\", which writes `top: 450px` on a 900px viewport and parks the band 422px down the screen where it never reaches the edge at all. A margin shifts the band's RESTING place (`marginTop` put it 16px lower) and not its stuck place, which stayed 0, so a sticky band floating below the top edge is not expressible: put the gap inside the band. (2) It sticks inside ITS PARENT's box, so the band must be a direct child of the tall page column; wrapped in a Group only as tall as itself it scrolls straight off, measured at top -305. (3) Any ancestor with Clip Content on kills it — the same -305, silently, with no error anywhere. (4) `zIndex` is structural here, not decoration: leave it off and the band's geometry is still right, top 0, while the section text paints straight through it, illegible, and takes the clicks — the sibling bands are position relative too, so DOM order wins without it. Prefer sticky to \"fixed\" for a header: fixed takes no space, so the page measured 1148px instead of 1205px — exactly one band shorter — with the first section starting underneath it. Unwrapped, the nav row is 463px wide and forces the layout viewport open at 390px, so the shell sets `flexWrap: \"wrap\"` and the band grows from 57px to 85px instead of overflowing.",
  "demonstrates": [
    "Group",
    "Page",
    "Text",
    "net.noodl.controls.button"
  ],
